  "diagnosis": [
    "A9.6 shows that global Head 2 loss scaling is too blunt for this UNSW hierarchy. It increased the total pressure on Head 2 but did not produce better family boundaries.",
    "The main Head 2 issue is not simply undertraining the shared encoder: binary macro-F1 and binary F1 improved, while attack-family macro-F1 and rare-class macro-F1 decreased.",
    "The routing profile worsened for attacks: missed attacks increased by 283 and correctly attributed attacks decreased by 437, while wrong-family detected attacks increased by 154.",
    "Weak and overlapping families did not benefit. Analysis, Backdoor, and DoS all had lower F1 under A9.6.",
    "Rare-class behavior became less balanced. Shellcode recall increased, but precision fell enough to reduce Shellcode F1 and rare-class macro-F1.",
    "The next change should target hard Head 2 examples or class boundaries directly rather than increasing attack_loss_weight further."
  ],
  "next_recommended_experiment": "head2_focal_loss",
  "next_experiment_rationale": [
